THE NINER'S — PLUGIN SPECIFICATION
==================================
A Klon Centaur-style overdrive for a Python plugin host that auto-discovers
modules exposing get_name, get_knobs, get_switches, and apply_effect.

PURPOSE
-------
Replace a simple volume-boost example with a three-path overdrive inspired by
the Klon Centaur: dual-gang gain (drive vs clean), constant bass feed-forward,
germanium-like hard clip after a mid-focused gain stage, then a treble shelf
and output volume. Display name is "The Niner's". Enclosure colors are gold,
red, and white (San Francisco 49ers palette).

HOST INTERFACE (MUST MATCH EXACTLY)
-----------------------------------
The host imports the module, instantiates the effect class, reads metadata,
writes live parameter attributes onto the instance, then calls apply_effect.

Required class name: VolumeBoost
  Some hosts look up this name. Do not rename the class. The GUI title comes
  from get_name(), not the class name.

Required dataclasses (copy as-is so the host can type-check / construct UI):

  @dataclass
  class KnobColorScheme:
      outline: str = "black"
      face: str = "white"
      needle: str = "black"

  @dataclass
  class Knob:
      name: str = "Generic"
      min: float = 0.0
      max: float = 1.0
      default: float = 0.5
      click_pts: List[float] = field(default_factory=lambda: [0.5])
      knob_color_scheme: KnobColorScheme = field(
          default_factory=lambda: KnobColorScheme(
              outline="black", face="white", needle="black"
          )
      )

  @dataclass
  class Switch:
      name: str = "Enable"
      default: bool = True

Required methods on VolumeBoost:

  get_name() -> str
      Return "The Niner's".

  get_colors() -> dict[str, str]
      Hex colors for the host skin. Required keys (same as the volume example):
        face, edge, text, muted, button, button_hot, button_on, button_text,
        switch_on, switch_off, slider, slider_handle, knob_outline, knob_face,
        knob_needle
      Intended values:
        face           #C8A44E   gold enclosure
        edge           #6B0000   dark red
        text           #F7F2E8   off-white
        muted          #F0D9A0
        button         #B00000
        button_hot     #D02020
        button_on      #B00000
        button_text    #F7F2E8
        switch_on      #B00000
        switch_off     #3A2208
        slider         #6B0000
        slider_handle  #F7F2E8
        knob_outline   #6B0000
        knob_face      #F7F2E8
        knob_needle    #B00000

  get_knobs() -> List[Knob]
      Three knobs, in this order:
        1. name="Gain"    min=0 max=1 default=0.55
           click_pts=[0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]
        2. name="Treble"  min=0 max=1 default=0.50
           click_pts=[0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]
        3. name="Volume"  min=0 max=1 default=0.70
           click_pts=[0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]
      Each uses KnobColorScheme(outline="#6B0000", face="#F7F2E8",
      needle="#B00000").

  get_switches() -> List[Switch]
      Four switches, in this order:
        1. name="Enable"   default=True    (bypass when False)
        2. name="Fat"      default=False   (more bass through drive + FF)
        3. name="Silicon"  default=False   (0.70 V clip instead of 0.35 V)
        4. name="Led"      default=False   (1.60 V clip; wins over Silicon)

  apply_effect(self, audio, sample_rate: int)
      audio: numpy array, nominally float in [-1, 1], shape (n,) or
      (n, channels). sample_rate: Hz, integer.
      Return an array with the same dtype and rank as the input. If Enable is
      off, return audio unchanged (same object is acceptable).

LIVE ATTRIBUTES THE HOST WRITES
-------------------------------
The host maps knob/switch names to instance attributes by lowercasing the
name. It sets these before each apply_effect call. Read them with getattr
and defaults so a missing write does not crash.

  self.gain      float 0..1   from knob "Gain"
  self.treble    float 0..1   from knob "Treble"
  self.volume    float 0..1   from knob "Volume"
  self.enable    bool         from switch "Enable"
  self.fat       bool         from switch "Fat"
  self.silicon   bool         from switch "Silicon"
  self.led       bool         from switch "Led"

Optional internals (not exposed as knobs):
  self.oversample   int, default 8
  self.input_volts  float, default 0.30   assumed guitar peak volts for
                                          a full-scale file sample of 1.0

Do not take a long parameter list on apply_effect. The volume example used
instance members; this plugin must do the same.

DEPENDENCIES
------------
Preferred (this spec's reference DSP): numpy and scipy.signal (butter,
sosfilt).
Fallback: numpy only, with one-pole IIR instead of Butterworth / biquad EQ.
If scipy is imported at module top and is missing, the host will fail to
load the plugin. Install with: python -m pip install numpy scipy
into the same interpreter that runs host.py.

CIRCUIT BEHAVIOR TO EMULATE
---------------------------
Not a full SPICE netlist. Reproduce these audible blocks of a Klon-style
path:

  1. Input high-pass ~18 Hz (coupling).
  2. Split into three paths.
  3. Drive path: high-pass ~120 Hz (~80 Hz if Fat), peaking EQ at 1 kHz
     with Q ~0.7 and gain 13 dB + 27 dB * Gain (about +13 to +40 dB),
     low-pass ~6.5 kHz, soft op-amp sat at +/-8.5 V, then diode clip,
     then another op-amp sat after *2.2.
  4. Bass feed-forward: 1-pole (or Butterworth-1) low-pass at 106 Hz
     (70 Hz if Fat), mix coefficient ~1.15 (1.25 if Fat). Always on;
     not inverse to Gain.
  5. Clean path: high-pass ~80 Hz, low-pass ~8 kHz. Mix amount falls as
     Gain rises (dual-gang).
  6. Sum: mix = Gain*drive + (1-Gain)*0.85*clean + 0.28*bass
  7. Tone: high shelf, hinge 408 Hz (280 Hz if Fat), shelf dB =
     (Treble - 0.45) * 22. Noon is slightly bright.
  8. Output high-pass ~12 Hz. Output scale 3.4 * (Volume ** 1.4)
     (audio-ish taper).
  9. Soft limit: tanh(y * 0.85) / 0.85 after converting volts back to
     normalized audio via / input_volts.

DIODE MODES
-----------
If Led:     Vf=1.60 V, softness=0.08
Elif Silicon: Vf=0.70 V, softness=0.05
Else:       Vf=0.35 V, softness=0.035   (1N34A-style germanium)

Clip: y = Vf * tanh((1/softness) * (x/Vf))
Op-amp: y = 8.5 * tanh(x/8.5)

Led overrides Silicon when both are on.

OVERSAMPLING (SCIPY REFERENCE)
------------------------------
Factor os = max(2, oversample), default 8.
Upsample: zero-stuff by os, scale inserted samples by os, then 8th-order
Butterworth low-pass at 0.45 * original_fs (designed at fs_os).
Run all nonlinear stages and tone at fs_os.
Before downsample: same 8th-order LPF at 0.45 * original_fs.
Downsample by taking every os-th sample.

Peak EQ and high shelf are RBJ cookbook SOS, run through sosfilt.

NUMPY-ONLY FALLBACK
-------------------
If scipy is forbidden: one-pole LP a = exp(-2*pi*fc/fs), b0 = 1-a,
y[n] = b0*x[n] + a*y[n-1]. HP = x - LP. Approximate the 1 kHz peak as
drive + 1.35 * LP1000(drive). Approximate the shelf as
low + (mix-low)*(1 + (Treble-0.45)*2.4). Drive linear gain
4.5 * 10**(1.15*Gain). Output 2.8 * (Volume**1.4). Same mix and diode
laws. No oversampling required in the fallback.

SIGNAL CONTRACT
---------------
Work in float64 internally. Scale input by input_volts before analog-domain
processing. Process each channel independently. Cast the result back to the
input dtype. Preserve mono as 1-D if the input was 1-D.

INIT DEFAULTS
-------------
self.name = "The Niner's"
self.gain = 0.55
self.treble = 0.50
self.volume = 0.70
self.enable = True
self.fat = False
self.silicon = False
self.led = False

DISCOVERY RULES
---------------
Do not import scipy unless it is installed; a failed top-level import
prevents loading.
Do not add extra public plugin classes that also define get_name /
get_knobs / apply_effect. Knob, Switch, and KnobColorScheme are data only.
Keep the volume-plugin method names and signatures. Do not add extra
required constructor arguments.

NON-GOALS
---------
Not a sample-accurate WDF or SPICE of every Klon resistor. Not a true-bypass
hardware buffer model beyond the input HPF. Not realtime-guaranteed; the
host may process whole buffers / files.

ACCEPTANCE CHECKS FOR ANOTHER IMPLEMENTATION
--------------------------------------------
1. Module imports in the host's Python.
2. VolumeBoost() constructs; get_name() is "The Niner's".
3. get_knobs() length 3; names Gain, Treble, Volume.
4. get_switches() length 4; names Enable, Fat, Silicon, Led.
5. get_colors() contains every key listed above.
6. enable=False returns audio unchanged.
7. gain near 0 is mostly clean + bass FF; gain near 1 is mostly clipped
   mid-forward drive.
8. fat=True is bassier. led=True clips later than germanium.
9. Output shape/dtype match input. Values stay roughly in [-1, 1] after
   the final tanh limiter.